---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const heading = "mb-2 text-base font-semibold";
const body = "mb-8 text-prose/[1.7] text-muted-foreground last:mb-0";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - Kaja"
  description="Kaja privacy policy. Kaja runs on your own machine or your own server, and sends no data to the Kaja maintainers."
>
  <section class="mx-auto w-full max-w-doc px-6 pt-16 pb-20 md:px-8 md:pt-20 md:pb-24">
    <h1 class="mb-2 font-display text-title font-semibold tracking-display">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mb-12 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: September 14, 2026</p>

    <h2 class={heading}>No data collection</h2>
    <p class={body}>
      Kaja does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data to the Kaja maintainers or to any third party. There is no account and nothing to sign up for.
    </p>

    <h2 class={heading}>Where Kaja runs</h2>
    <p class={body}>
      Kaja is a desktop app you install on your own machine, or a container you run on your own server. Either way it is your installation: the configuration,
      your scripts and your credentials stay where you put them, and no server operated by the Kaja maintainers is involved.
    </p>

    <h2 class={heading}>Service connections</h2>
    <p class={body}>
      Calls to the gRPC, OpenAPI, MCP and Twirp services you configure go to those services. Kaja carries the call — from your machine on the desktop, from your
      own server in the container — so the traffic passes through your installation and nowhere else. Nothing is logged or stored beyond the run history the app
      keeps locally so you can read a response again.
    </p>

    <h2 class={heading}>The hosted demo</h2>
    <p class={body}>
      The demo at{" "}
      <a href="https://demo.kaja.tools" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">demo.kaja.tools</a> is the one Kaja the
      maintainers run, and calls you make there pass through it. It is there to try Kaja against the demo services; use your own installation for anything of your
      own.
    </p>

    <h2 class={heading}>Analytics and tracking</h2>
    <p class={body}>Kaja does not include any analytics, telemetry, or tracking of any kind.</p>

    <h2 class={heading}>Contact</h2>
    <p class={body}>
      If you have questions about this policy, you can open an issue on{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/wham/kaja" class="text-foreground underline underline-offset-3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
